fact WorkItem(id: "WI-573", description: some(value: "Guarded-effect guard discharge over spec-op / type-directed guards (CONSUMER of the WI-502 typed-term substrate). Extend the WI-067 discharge from native-scalar guards (eq(b,0) over Int64) to guards whose predicate is a spec op ({ Error :- eq(b,0) } over a non-native carrier; { Error[EmptyStream] :- isEmpty(s) }) by refuting them through the carried type on the argument: a concrete carrier (typed value) dispatches the spec op via its requires dictionary (runtime monomorphization), making the guard evaluable/refutable; an abstract carrier stays present (sound). Depends on WI-502. Unblocks WI-567 (concrete head discharge) and WI-566 (048 Phase-4 discharge over rule-defined predicates). RE-SCOPED 2026-06-27 from Shape A monomorphization (dropped). See docs/design/constrained-term-substrate.md. Acceptance: cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-572", "WI-578", "WI-592"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-29T13:46:21Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-573", name: "wi502")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-573", author: "claude", content: "UNCLAIMED + RE-WIRED (post-2026-06-27 session): the 2026-06-27T04:09 claim predated the 06:42/08:08 re-scope that DROPPED this ticket's old 'Shape A monomorphization' scope, so the claim was stale. Now depends on WI-578 (typed-VALUE carrier) -- guard discharge dispatches the spec op via the concrete carrier's requires dictionary, which needs the typed-value. Resume after WI-578 lands.", at: "2026-06-27T20:29:03Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-573", author: "claude", content: "Prerequisite WI-592 DELIVERED (constructor args now decidable in Γ-discharge: try_occurrence_to_term lowers a constructor var_ref→Ref; substitute_ref_syms no longer recurses into var_ref). REMAINING WI-573 SCOPE (Layer 2, verified by probe): a guard whose predicate is a spec op resolves to the generic anthill.prelude.Eq.eq, which is ALSO a registered structural builtin (BuiltinTag::Eq). So a NATIVE-Eq carrier (structural, no override) now discharges soundly via the builtin (post-WI-592). But a carrier with a CUSTOM eq override discharges via the STRUCTURAL builtin too — UNSOUND (ignores the override). The SLD resolver does NOT dispatch user spec-op overrides (confirmed: dispatch is a typer/eval concern, resolve.rs only handles Eq.eq/Eq.neq builtins). So WI-573 = detect when the carrier overrides the spec op and either (a) dispatch the guard goal to the carrier impl via the carried type (value_type_term, WI-578) = runtime monomorphization, or (b) suspend (keep effect) when an override exists but can't be dispatched. The isEmpty/head CASCADE (isEmpty default body calls splitFirst, another spec op) = WI-567, not WI-573. ALSO: the occurrence-twin substitute_ref_syms_occ lacks the var_ref skip WI-592 added to the term path — benign/pre-existing (guard goals are Value::Term so untriggered), worth symmetry if a Node-carried guard ever stores a re-keyable var_ref.", at: "2026-06-29T06:57:26Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-573", author: "claude", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-29 (commit f8e4dd7, full workspace suite green) — the SOUND FLOOR (ticket option (b)): detect a custom eq/neq override and SUSPEND (keep the effect), do NOT let the structural Eq/Neq builtin decide it. THE HAZARD is exactly the eq/neq family: negate_goal swaps eq<->neq into a POSITIVE goal the structural builtin DECIDES; every other predicate negates via not(..) which prove_from_gamma's definite_only already suppresses (kept soundly — so isEmpty/head guards were never the unsound-DROP path; that cascade = WI-567, the DISCHARGE side). New gate in guarded_atom_refuted (typing.rs): for an eq/neq conjunct, scan BOTH operands' FULL value structure (value_carrier_overrides_eq_family_deep mirrors views_structurally_equal's positional + named recursion) and suspend if ANY reachable carrier has its own eq/neq member (carrier_override_op). Extracted eq_neq_functors shared with negate_goal so swap+gate can't diverge. 7 tests (top-level keep / native drop / declarable / conservative-suspend-not-dispatch / nested-element keep / nested-field keep / nested-native drop). /code-review (high) caught the NESTED-carrier hole (a top-level-only check missed eq(some(Green),some(Red)) over Option[Color] = unsound drop) -> fixed via the deep scan; reuse finding -> eq_neq_functors. DEFERRED (option (a)): runtime-monomorphization DISPATCH of the override so a custom-override guard can still DISCHARGE (not just suspend) — this is the discharge capability WI-567/WI-566 need. RESIDUAL (separate, review Finding C): the direct prove_from_gamma sites (typing.rs ~3669, proof_verify.rs ~602) decide eq over a custom carrier structurally too — a potential soundness gap in the WI-538/WI-558 PROOF paths, out of WI-573's guarded-effect-discharge scope, candidate follow-on.", at: "2026-06-29T13:46:13Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-573", author: "claude", content: "FOLLOW-ONS NOW FILED (2026-07-18). This ticket's two deferrals were prose-only and untracked; they are now tickets. (1) The DEFERRED 'option (a)' (runtime-monomorphization dispatch so a custom-override guard can DISCHARGE, not just suspend) = WI-755. IMPORTANT UPDATE TO THIS TICKET'S PREMISE: option (a) is no longer 'build the dispatch' — WI-616 (delivered 2026-07-03, with WI-625/628/664) already built it, making eq/neq semantic (BuiltinTag::SemEq/SemNeq -> sem_eq_core, resolve.rs:4010; sem_eq_dispatch at :4168 already implements dispatch-on-ground / delay-on-buried-override, and its doc cites 'the WI-573 reasoning' by name). So the sound floor delivered HERE — guard_conjunct_overrides_structural_eq, called from conjunct_refuted (typing.rs ~21503) — has become STALE: it short-circuits before refute_guard -> prove_from_gamma -> resolver, shadowing the very dispatch it was written to wait for. WI-755 is therefore 'retire/narrow the gate', not 'implement dispatch'. (2) The RESIDUAL 'review Finding C' (direct prove_from_gamma sites deciding eq structurally over a custom carrier) = WI-756. Finding C's line numbers have drifted ('typing.rs ~3669' is now 5471) and it MISSED a third site: precondition_proved (typing.rs:21871, WI-539), the positive dual of precondition_refuted (:21893) which DOES route through the gated conjunct_refuted — so the two polarities are asymmetric today. WI-756 covers all three sites (typing.rs:5471 WI-538 'by derivation', typing.rs:21871 WI-539 requires, proof_verify.rs:602 WI-558 ensures); the gap likely closed indirectly via WI-616, making it characterization-and-regression work unless a path is found deciding structurally. ORDERING: WI-756 comes FIRST and WI-755 depends on it — WI-756 confirms the exact premise WI-755 relies on (that SemEq decides correctly through prove_from_gamma), so verifying it de-risks removing the gate. WI-566 and WI-567 now also depend on WI-755: they listed only this delivered ticket and so read as UNBLOCKED, but the discharge capability they need is WI-755, not the suspend-only floor delivered here.", at: "2026-07-18T13:43:25Z")
